> Conclusion

Scaled residual branches preserve an identity contribution to input derivatives while scaling
the learned correction and its parameter derivatives. Full block counts and the final C-block
exception remain explicit. The compact CIFAR-10 fits use supervised auxiliary heads
and report held-out predictions from their validation-selected checkpoints.

> References

- [Szegedy et al. (2017), Inception-v4, Inception-ResNet and the Impact of Residual Connections on Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.07261).
- [TF-Slim Inception v4](https://github.com/tensorflow/models/blob/master/research/slim/nets/inception_v4.py).
- [TF-Slim Inception-ResNet-v2](https://github.com/tensorflow/models/blob/master/research/slim/nets/inception_resnet_v2.py).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset and binary-file layout](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
